Subject: Tweak: Super Team
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

Super Mario Strikers (GameCube) has a hidden robot team, the Super Team. Charged
has no such model, but the GameCube game's robot (art/characters/SuperTeam)
uses the same skeleton as Charged's characters. With "Super Team" enabled, the
captain and sidekicks of the chosen team look like those robots.

The port makes, from the player's Super Mario Strikers disc, a robot version of
each character model of a robot class as it loads: the robot fitted to that
character's bones and size, in the character's own material with the robot's
textures (src/platform/super_team.cpp). It has its own model id, and only the
robot players get those ids: a character on both teams keeps its own look on
the other one. The electrocution and shadow models, skeleton, animations and
play stay the character's. Bowser, Petey Piranha and Boo keep their look; their
bodies fit no humanoid robot.

